{"name":"Echoes of Love","hex":"#eededd","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"echoes","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of echo"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of echo"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/echoes"},{"term":"love","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep caring for the existence of another.","Strong affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have a strong affection for (someone or something).","To need, thrive on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love"}],"entries":[{"title":"Echoes of Love (The Doobie Brothers song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Echoes of Love\" is a song by the American rock band The Doobie Brothers. The song was written by band member Patrick Simmons in collaboration with Willie Mitchell and Earl Randle. This song served as the second single from their seventh studio album Livin' on the Fault Line."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/cd/Echoes_of_Love_%28The_Doobie_Brothers_song%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Echoes_of_Love_(The_Doobie_Brothers_song)"},{"title":"Love","blocks":[{"text":"Love encompasses a range of strong and positive emotional and mental states, from the most sublime virtue or good habit, the deepest interpersonal affection, to the simplest pleasure. An example of this range of meanings is that the love of a mother differs from the love of a spouse, which differs from the love for food. Most commonly, love refers to a feeling of strong attraction and emotional attachment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/cd/Echoes_of_Love_%28The_Doobie_Brothers_song%29.jpg/250px-Echoes_of_Love_%28The_Doobie_Brothers_song%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upl